---
description: A PR does not go out with work it names as not done, or a result it cannot explain
alwaysApply: true
---

# No open ends in a PR

A PR is opened when its work is finished, not when it runs. Two sentences do not belong in a PR body or in a report to the owner:

- "Not measured." A PR that claims speed or memory (fewer allocations while building SQL, a faster result mapper) measures it before it is opened, against a named baseline, and reports the numbers before and after (`.cursor/rules/bench.mdc`). What is left is stated with a number and the reason it stays.
- "The cause is not confirmed." A result the agent cannot explain (an integration test that fails one run in ten, a dialect that returns a different row count or type from the others, a SQL golden mismatch) is traced to its cause from the data before the PR is opened. A guess is not written as an explanation, with or without "probably".

What is out of the row's scope is a roadmap row that names when (`.cursor/rules/defer.mdc`), not a caveat. A finding about code the row did not change becomes its own Issue at once (`.cursor/rules/pace.mdc`).

A CI failure that does not come back on the next runs is not explained by the reruns. When its log does not show the cause, the PR says that the cause was not found and what was read, and a change that makes the test steadier keeps it failing on the fault it guards (shown with a mutant). #95 wrote a single 536-byte difference on macOS as a recompilation of the JIT, which nothing had shown.

A reason written as likely ("probably", 「と考えられる」) is checked first when a cheap check exists: reading the generated SQL with `ToSql()`, reading the database's documentation or its log, one more run.

A comment in the code is held to the same line: it says what was observed, and marks a cause that was not confirmed as not confirmed, with the Issue number.

```text
# BAD
PostgreSQL だけ統合テストがたまに落ちますが、おそらくコンテナの起動待ちの問題です。性能は測っていません。

# GOOD
PostgreSQL の統合テストは 20 回中 3 回失敗した。サーバーログを見ると、失敗はすべて前のテストの
トランザクションが未コミットのまま同じ行を UPDATE していた回だった。テストごとに接続を分けて 50 回連続で通過。
SELECT 1 本の SQL 生成は 1.9 → 0.6 µs、確保は 1,240 → 312 B（BenchmarkDotNet、main 比）。
```
